rates."},{"choice_key":"B","choice_text":"0.491","is_correct":false,"rationale":"Uses π/4 rather than π/8 as the cross-sectional factor."},{"choice_key":"C","choice_text":"0.982","is_correct":false,"rationale":"Uses the full-circle area with the given diameter."},{"choice_key":"D","choice_text":"1.963","is_correct":false,"rationale":"Treats the diameter as the radius and uses a full circle."}],"canonical_answers":["A"],"parts":[{"part_key":"question","ordinal":1,"prompt":"The base of a solid is 0≤x≤1.5 and 0≤y≤e^(−x²). Cross sections perpendicular to the x-axis are semicircles whose diameters lie in the base. What is the volume, to the nearest thousandth?\n\nA. 0.245\nB. 0.491\nC. 0.982\nD. 1.963","stimulus_refs":["directions"],"response_modalities":["choice"],"points":1,"criteria":[{"criterion_key":"correct-answer","points":1,"description":"Select the unique correct response.","required_evidence":["A","A semicircle with diameter e^(−x²) has area (π/8)e^(−2x²), so V=(π/8)∫₀^1.5e^(−2x²)dx≈0.245."],"accepted_variants":["Only a displayed choice that is mathematically identical to the keyed response may be treated as equivalent."],"insufficient_responses":["An unkeyed choice without a valid ambiguity finding."],"contradictions":["A choice or rationale that conflicts with the governing domain, units, or theorem conditions."],"minimum_fix":"Select the keyed response after correcting the first invalid mathematical step.","deterministic_checks":[{"check_type":"choice-key","parameters":{"correct_key":"A"}}]}]}],"review_notes":{"expected_reasoning":"A semicircle with diameter e^(−x²) has area (π/8)e^(−2x²), so V=(π/8)∫₀^1.5e^(−2x²)dx≈0.245.","teaching_explanation":"A semicircle with diameter e^(−x²) has area (π/8)e^(−2x²), so V=(π/8)∫₀^1.5e^(−2x²)dx≈0.245.","minimum_fix":"Correct the first invalid mathematical step, then recompute without changing the problem conditions.","transfer_candidate":"Create a new item assessing Topic 8.8 with different values and a different represe